# MySQL

Enforcement: **B**. Verify engine (InnoDB vs others) and major version.

## Distinctives

- InnoDB row locking + gap locks depending on isolation level.
- `REPEATABLE READ` default on many deployments — know phantom behavior.
- Online DDL support varies by version and operation; check before production alter.
- Character sets/collations affect uniqueness and comparisons — be explicit (utf8mb4).
- Careful with `GROUP BY` / ONLY_FULL_GROUP_BY modes.

## Do not

- Assume PostgreSQL DDL/lock semantics
- Ignore charset conversions in migrations
